# Scoped rule index

These rules load when their files are read. Open the rule first when the task matches but no
file of theirs is in context.

- Store build or submit steps, EAS, store identity → `mobile-store-builds-on-demand`,
  `mobile-next-store-identity`
- About or Summary content → `about-summary-web-mobile-alignment`
- Naming description, About, or Summary fields, sections, or catalog keys → `domain-terms`
- Playlist versus HLS playlist (m3u8) naming or searches → `domain-terms`
- A feature needs a `podcast:*` tag the namespace lacks, or a namespace change draft →
  `podcast-namespace-proposals`
- Mobile run, install, or device commands → `mobile-ios-simulator`
- Mobile terminal tabs, CarPlay logs, or Expo CLI → `vscode-terminals-mobile`
- Any ship step (tag, release, publish, store, promotion) → `release-notes-suggest`
- Comments in source, tests, SQL, or styles → `comments-future-forward`
- UI labels, titles, buttons, or catalog copy → `ui-copy-casing`
- Membership expiry, notifications, scheduled jobs → `no-membership-expiry-notifications`
- `sync-develop-to-staging.sh`, `sync-staging-to-main.sh`, `update-lockfile-linux.sh`, or
  `bump-version.sh` → `reinstall-node-modules-after-linux-npm` (these leave host `node_modules`
  alone; do not add a reinstall step)
- Legacy app, podverse-rn, or v4 mobile → `legacy-app-reference`
- v4 / OGen API, entities, or prod-copy database (`V4_DATABASE_URL`) → `v4-backend-reference`
- Popularity tracking, Taste Profile consent, listener ids, stats or taste tables →
  `popularity-listener-id-separation`
- Adding or changing an authenticated API route, or a rate-limit wrapper that authenticates →
  `api-key-route-access`
- Stacked headings, paragraphs, buttons, dividers, or other block copy → `even-content-spacing`
- A new dynamic detail page in `apps/web`, or a server fetch for the entity a page renders →
  `web-detail-route-not-found`
- Notification `Last-Event-ID` replay, the iOS livestream rewind scrubber, landscape video Exit,
  or the cross-device "Sending to…" status → `e2e-problematic-assertions`
